CloudBurrow patch 56 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1458). Applies after patch 0050; needs patch
0030.

Patch 0030 gave a table made by CREATE TABLE with a column list the
pseudo-column _PARTITION_STREAMED, the time CloudBurrow's front streamed
a row, which DML reads to refuse a row streamed in the last 30 minutes;
a table made by CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT got none, so its streamed
rows were held from DML only while in the streaming buffer. It now gets
the column too, NULL on the rows the SELECT gives (none of them was
streamed); not a temporary table, which tabledata.insertAll cannot
stream to, nor CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, which may name a table made
without it. ctas_streamed_at_column_test.go fails without the patch and
passes with it.

